 "girdle": {
  "why": "Scapulohumeral rhythm, the clavicle and the scapula driven from the humerus (rig_drive.girdle): tables of the arm's elevation A (deg from the torso's down axis), monotone C1 cubics flat past the ends, each relative to its value at the rest (MakeHuman's A-pose, A0 ~43 deg; the rest exactly neutral). Clavicle elevation and retraction: Ludewig, Phadke, Braman et al. 2009 (JBJS 91-A, 3D motion of the shoulder complex in 12 subjects: clavicle elevation ~10-15 deg, retraction ~15-30 deg, scapular upward rotation ~40-50 deg, posterior tilt ~20-30 deg over full elevation) and Inman, Saunders and Abbott 1944 (the setting phase: through the first ~30 deg the girdle barely moves, so the curves are nearly flat from 0 (hanging) to A0 and a hanging arm moves the clavicle and blade only a little down from rest). Protraction with forward reach (10 deg per unit of the arm's direction . front beyond rest) and the blade's forward glide (15 mm per unit) as the arm flexes forward (Ludewig 2009: scapular protraction in flexion). The upper arm keeps its world turn (the clip's aim).",
