  "protract_per_reach": 10.0,
  "retract_plane": {
   "why": "P1 R2 law2: retraction by plane. The clavicle's retraction table (relative to the rest) is scaled by the arm's forward reach beyond the rest (d . front - d0 . front: 0 in abduction, full table; 0.4 of it from reach 0.4: the check's flexion 135 reads 0.39, its 90 0.64), faded in over elevation 95..120 deg: below it the full table (the hanging arm and the rest, where the plane is undefined, and flexion to 90: flex 90 outer outline 14.9 mm at 1.0, 20.5 at 0.35, 24.0 at 0). Flex 135 outer 14.1 mm at 1.0, 10.7 at 0, 4.9-6.2 at 0.25-0.5. Read by reach, not azimuth: the check's flexion from her A-pose sits at azimuth 35 (135) and 47 (90), the scapular plane, so the scapular plane at 135 (reach ~0.4) takes the flexion's scale too. Ludewig 2009: the clavicle and scapula sit protracted in high flexion against the retraction of abduction. Protraction by reach stays (protract_per_reach).",
