   "why": "P1 R2 law2: the share's hanging branch. amount 0.5 of the arm's turn beyond the clavicle when the arm is above the rest elevation (the cap turns with the humerus as it lifts); below.amount when it hangs below the rest (the deltoid's top stays under the acromion, riding the girdle), smoothstep-blended over the rest -+ band deg (no pop). Tuned by the arm_hang panel (top-drop ratio at 5 deg: 0.5 -> -0.54, 0.15 -> 0.04, 0 -> 0.54, -0.03 -> 0.84, -0.1 -> 0.99); the cost is the inner upper arm's known contact with the torso side 6-11 cm below the joint (1.9 -> ~9 mm deep at 5 deg)."
